┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   JENKINS DEVSECOPS PIPELINE            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

STAGE 1 — PRE-FLIGHT
─────────────────────
  ├── Validate branch naming convention
  ├── Check commit message format
  ├── Detect changed services
  └── Notify pipeline start (Slack/Email)

STAGE 2 — SECRET DETECTION (FAIL FAST)
────────────────────────────────────────
  ├── GitLeaks — scan full git history
  ├── TruffleHog — deep secret scanning
  └── ❌ BLOCK pipeline if secrets found

STAGE 3 — DEPENDENCY SECURITY AUDIT
─────────────────────────────────────
  ├── npm audit (user-service)         HIGH/CRITICAL block
  ├── pip-audit (order, auth, notify)  HIGH/CRITICAL block
  ├── govulncheck (inventory-service)  HIGH/CRITICAL block
  ├── OWASP Dependency Check (payment) CVSS >= 9 block
  └── composer audit (analytics)       HIGH/CRITICAL block

STAGE 4 — SAST (Static Analysis)
──────────────────────────────────
  ├── Bandit (Python services)
  ├── Semgrep (all languages — OWASP Top 10)
  ├── ESLint Security Plugin (Node.js)
  ├── SpotBugs + Find Security Bugs (Java)
  ├── golangci-lint (Go)
  └── PHPCS Security Audit (PHP)

STAGE 5 — CODE QUALITY
───────────────────────
  ├── SonarQube analysis (all services)
  ├── Code coverage thresholds
  ├── Complexity metrics
  ├── Duplication detection
  └── Quality Gate — block if fails

STAGE 6 — UNIT & INTEGRATION TESTS
─────────────────────────────────────
  ├── user-service      → Jest
  ├── order-service     → Pytest
  ├── inventory-service → Go test
  ├── payment-service   → JUnit/Maven
  ├── analytics-service → PHPUnit
  ├── auth-service      → Pytest
  └── notification-service → Pytest

STAGE 7 — BUILD DOCKER IMAGES
───────────────────────────────
  ├── Build only changed services
  ├── Tag with: git SHA + branch + semver
  └── Store image digests for scanning

STAGE 8 — CONTAINER SECURITY SCAN
────────────────────────────────────
  ├── Trivy — CVE scanning (CRITICAL block)
  ├── Grype — second opinion scanner
  ├── Docker Bench Security
  ├── Hadolint — Dockerfile best practices
  └── ❌ BLOCK if CRITICAL CVEs found

STAGE 9 — INFRASTRUCTURE SECURITY
────────────────────────────────────
  ├── Checkov — K8s manifests (CIS benchmark)
  ├── Kubesec — Kubernetes security scoring
  ├── kube-score — K8s best practices
  ├── Checkov — Docker Compose
  └── OPA/Conftest — policy as code

STAGE 10 — DAST (Dynamic Analysis)
─────────────────────────────────────
  ├── Spin up services in Docker Compose
  ├── OWASP ZAP — active scan all endpoints
  ├── Nuclei — vulnerability templates
  ├── API fuzzing (auth endpoints)
  └── Tear down test environment

STAGE 11 — COMPLIANCE & REPORTING
────────────────────────────────────
  ├── Generate SBOM (Software Bill of Materials)
  │     └── Syft — CycloneDX format
  ├── Aggregate all security reports
  ├── Publish to DefectDojo (vulnerability mgmt)
  ├── Generate HTML security report
  └── Archive all artifacts

STAGE 12 — PUSH TO REGISTRY
──────────────────────────────
  ├── Only if ALL security gates pass
  ├── Only on develop/main branches
  ├── Push to Docker Hub
  ├── Sign images (Docker Content Trust)
  └── Update image tags in K8s manifests

STAGE 13 — DEPLOY
───────────────────
  ├── develop → staging namespace
  ├── main    → production namespace
  ├── kubectl apply all manifests
  ├── Wait for rollout completion
  └── Smoke tests post-deploy

STAGE 14 — POST-DEPLOY VERIFICATION
──────────────────────────────────────
  ├── Health check all endpoints
  ├── Verify JWT authentication works
  ├── Test Kafka event chain
  ├── Check all pods Running
  └── Notify success/failure (Slack/Email)